TIP:  For the opening play a regular (C) and cover the 1st string of the 3rd fret with your pinky to 5th fret to cover note <g>.  Strum aiming for the covered 5th string <c> and then strum down to snap the 1st string.  Repeat.  Or ignore it and just play (C).

TIP:  If transposing, play the transposed (CaddG) root chord and add the 5th note if needed.

      
